<b>Madonna - Hard Candy: Instrumentals (2008) <b>| </b>AAC 256kbps / 48kHz</b><br>
<br>
<i><b>Hard Candy</b></i> is the eleventh <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Studio_album" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">studio album</a> by American singer and songwriter <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Madonna</a>. Released by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warner_Bros._Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Warner Bros. Records</a> on April 18, 2008, it was her last album for the company after a 25-year history until <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confessions_II" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Confessions II</a></i> (2026).<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_Candy_(Madonna_album)#cite_note-people-1" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">[1]</a> Madonna began working on <i>Hard Candy</i> in early 2007, and collaborated with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Justin Timberlake</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbaland" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Timbaland</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Neptunes" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">the Neptunes</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danja_(record_producer)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Nate "Danja" Hills</a> to produce a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance-pop" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">dance-pop</a> album incorporating <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip_hop_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">hip hop</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electropop" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">electropop</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">disco</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electro_(music)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">electro</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">funk</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_R&amp;B" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">R&amp;B</a>.<br>
